1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,357
In 1992, thousands of Brits bought

2
00:00:02,357 --> 00:00:04,296
vacuum cleaners they didn't need...

3
00:00:04,296 --> 00:00:06,162
just to fly to America for free.

4
00:00:06,162 --> 00:00:09,239
Hoover's offer: spend £100,

5
00:00:09,239 --> 00:00:11,921
get two free return flights to Europe.

6
00:00:11,921 --> 00:00:14,279
Then it added New York and Orlando.

7
00:00:14,279 --> 00:00:18,029
The cheapest vacuum that qualified cost £119.

8
00:00:18,029 --> 00:00:20,058
The tickets were worth a LOT more.

9
00:00:20,058 --> 00:00:21,788
People did the math.

10
00:00:21,788 --> 00:00:25,915
By March 1993, about 200,000 had claimed flights.

11
00:00:25,915 --> 00:00:28,167
Travel agents couldn't keep up.

12
00:00:28,167 --> 00:00:30,246
One angry customer went all the way to Iowa

13
00:00:30,246 --> 00:00:32,390
to confront the owner, Maytag.

14
00:00:32,390 --> 00:00:34,166
Maytag paid for charter planes,

15
00:00:34,166 --> 00:00:36,140
fired three Hoover bosses...

16
00:00:36,140 --> 00:00:40,005
and took about $60 million in charges in 1993.

17
00:00:40,005 --> 00:00:42,372
Two years later, it sold Hoover Europe.

18
00:00:42,372 --> 00:00:43,521
Hoover thought it was giving

19
00:00:43,521 --> 00:00:45,489
away flights to sell vacuums.

20
00:00:45,489 --> 00:00:47,138
But people were buying vacuums...

21
00:00:47,138 --> 00:00:48,320
to get the flights.
